{"title":"Market stall bake quantities","genre":"analysis","brief":"Complete the following real project in the current, initially empty directory. Choose the deliverables, media, tools, structure and implementation that serve the intended user. Build usable artifacts and check your work. Deliver the project itself. Omit personally identifying credits, author signatures and model or toolchain identity labels. No network access or credentials are provided.\n\nA Saturday market baker needs starting quantities for muffins and scones. Fictional historical data for six consecutive markets give baked/sold pairs. Muffins: 40/35, 40/40, 48/45, 48/48, 56/49, 56/52. Scones: 32/28, 32/30, 32/32, 40/35, 40/34, 40/38. Muffins sell for $4 and cost $1.20 each to make. Scones sell for $3.50 and cost $1.05 each. Unsold goods bring no revenue. Next market allows 88 items total, baked in batches of eight by product. Compare waste and contribution, flag what sellouts hide about demand, and evaluate candidate batch mixes. Start from an empty directory and choose offline deliverables the baker can reuse.","works":{"705ddae4f0edefd1":{"files":[{"name":"market-planner.html","bytes":8499,"sha256":"4db1309795d022ad76b7b335b40d391361e07d96c093f50fe39ad0386a089cd9","kind":"text","body":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Saturday bake planner</title>\n<style>\n*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f6f2e8;color:#252c22;font:16px/1.5 \"Avenir Next\",\"Helvetica Neue\",sans-serif}main{max-width:1000px;margin:auto;padding:36px 24px 64px}h1,h2,h3,p{margin:0}h1,h2,.qty{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:normal}h1{font-size:clamp(38px,7vw,70px);letter-spacing:-.05em;line-height:1.1}header{border-top:5px solid #284d3d;padding:22px 0}header p,.sub{color:#565b50}section,details{margin-top:28px}h2{font-size:30px;line-height:1.25;margin-bottom:8px}.plan{background:#284d3d;color:#fff9e9;padding:24px 28px;border-radius:5px}.plan h2{font-family:inherit;font-size:18px;font-weight:600}.pair{display:flex;gap:clamp(30px,10vw,100px);margin:8px 0 18px}.qty{font-size:clamp(44px,8vw,72px);line-height:1.1}.plan p{border-top:1px solid #719383;padding-top:14px}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:12px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}th,td{text-align:right;padding:9px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid #d3cfc0}th{font-size:13px;vertical-align:bottom}th:first-child,td:first-child{text-align:left}tr.best{background:#dde9da}label{display:inline-block;margin:9px 14px 4px 0}select,button,textarea{font:inherit;color:inherit}select,button{background:#fffdf6;border:1px solid #8d9586;border-radius:4px;padding:6px 9px}button,summary,select{cursor:pointer}summary{font-weight:650}textarea{display:block;width:100%;max-width:460px;font-family:monospace;background:#fffdf6;padding:10px}details{border-top:1px solid #b8b9a9;padding-top:14px}.note{margin-top:12px}.small{font-size:14px}.controls{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:3px 12px}.error{color:#912e23}button{margin-top:10px} @media(max-width:550px){main{padding:18px 14px 40px}th,td{padding:7px 5px}.scroll{font-size:14px}}@media print{body{background:white}main{padding:0}.plan{background:white;color:black;border:1px solid}.controls,details.editor{display:none}section,table,.plan{break-inside:avoid}}\n</style>\n<main><header><h1>Saturday bake planner</h1><p>Market capacity &nbsp;88 items &nbsp;·&nbsp; 8 items per batch</p></header>\n<section class=\"plan\" aria-live=\"polite\"><h2>Starting quantities</h2><div class=\"pair\"><div><span class=\"qty\" id=\"muffins\"></span><br>Muffins</div><div><span class=\"qty\" id=\"scones\"></span><br>Scones</div></div><p id=\"result\"></p></section>\n<section><h2>Compare the mixes</h2><p class=\"sub\">Each mix faces every recorded Saturday once. Figures are averages per market. Contribution covers revenue less the cost of everything baked.</p>\n<div class=\"controls\"><label>Capacity rule <select id=\"rule\"><option value=\"cap\">Up to 88 items</option><option value=\"full\">Exactly 88 items</option></select></label>\n<label>Extra demand per sellout <select id=\"extra\"><option value=\"0\">0 items (observed sales)</option><option value=\"4\">4 items</option><option value=\"8\">8 items</option></select></label></div>\n<p id=\"scenario\" class=\"note small\"></p>\n<div class=\"scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th>Muffins</th><th>Scones</th><th>Total baked</th><th>Avg. sold</th><th>Avg. waste</th><th>Avg. contribution</th></tr></thead><tbody id=\"mixes\"></tbody></table></div>\n<button id=\"more\"></button><p class=\"note\" id=\"trade\"></p></section>\n<section><h2>What the stall recorded</h2><p id=\"n\" class=\"sub\"></p><div class=\"scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>Baked</th><th>Sold</th><th>Waste</th><th>Waste %</th><th>Contribution</th><th>Sellouts</th></tr></thead><tbody id=\"history\"></tbody></table></div>\n<p class=\"note\">Selling the last item gives a lower bound on demand. The till records everyone who bought one and misses customers who arrived after it ran out. The extra-demand setting tests that uncertainty by adding units only to a product that sold out on that Saturday.</p>\n<p class=\"note small sub\">The replay treats the markets as equally likely, assumes customers keep their product choice, and gives leftovers zero revenue. Each muffin sells for $4.00 and costs $1.20 to bake. Each scone sells for $3.50 and costs $1.05. Contribution is before stall fees, labour and other overhead.</p></section>\n<details class=\"editor\"><summary>View or update market records</summary><p class=\"note\">Enter one Saturday per line, oldest first. Use four comma-separated whole numbers in the order shown. Apply changes to recalculate.</p>\n<label for=\"records\">Muffins baked, muffins sold, scones baked, scones sold</label><textarea id=\"records\" rows=\"8\" spellcheck=\"false\"></textarea><button id=\"apply\">Apply records</button><p id=\"status\" role=\"status\"></p></details>\n<noscript>This planner needs JavaScript enabled in your browser.</noscript></main>\n<script>\n'use strict';\nconst el=id=>document.getElementById(id);\nconst initial='40,35,32,28\\n40,40,32,30\\n48,45,32,32\\n48,48,40,35\\n56,49,40,34\\n56,52,40,38';\nconst storageKey='saturday-bake-records-v1';\nconst cash=cents=>'$'+(cents/100).toFixed(2);\nconst avg=num=>Number(num.toFixed(2)).toString();\nconst row=(cells,cls='')=>'<tr class=\"'+cls+'\">'+cells.map(c=>'<td>'+c+'</td>').join('')+'</tr>';\nfunction parseRecords(raw){\n const lines=raw.trim().split(/\\r?\\n/);\n return lines.map((line,i)=>{\n  const fields=line.split(',').map(x=>x.trim());\n  const nums=fields.map(Number);\n  if(fields.length!==4 || fields.some(x=>!/^\\d+$/.test(x)) || nums.some(x=>!Number.isSafeInteger(x)) || nums[1]>nums[0] || nums[3]>nums[2])\n   throw Error('Check line '+(i+1)+'. Enter four nonnegative whole numbers. Sold must be at most baked.');\n  return nums;\n });\n}\nlet raw=initial;\ntry{const saved=localStorage.getItem(storageKey);if(saved){parseRecords(saved);raw=saved}}catch{}\nlet records=parseRecords(raw),expanded=false;\nel('records').value=raw;\nfunction render(){\n const days=records.length, extra=Number(el('extra').value);\n const demand=records.map(([mb,ms,sb,ss])=>[ms+(mb>0&&ms===mb?extra:0),ss+(sb>0&&ss===sb?extra:0)]);\n const mixes=[];\n for(let m=0;m<=88;m+=8){\n  for(let s=0;s<=88-m;s+=8){\n   if(el('rule').value==='full'&&m+s!==88)continue;\n   let sold=0,net=0;\n   for(const [md,sd] of demand){\n    const a=Math.min(m,md),b=Math.min(s,sd);\n    sold+=a+b;net+=400*a+350*b-120*m-105*s;\n   }\n   mixes.push({m,s,total:m+s,sold:sold/days,waste:m+s-sold/days,net:net/days});\n  }\n }\n mixes.sort((a,b)=>b.net-a.net||a.waste-b.waste||a.m-b.m);\n const best=mixes[0];\n el('muffins').textContent=best.m;el('scones').textContent=best.s;\n el('result').textContent=best.m/8+' muffin batches + '+best.s/8+' scone batches use '+best.total+' of 88 spaces. Average contribution is '+cash(best.net)+' with '+avg(best.waste)+' items left over.';\n el('scenario').textContent=extra?'Sensitivity test assuming '+extra+' additional requests at each recorded product sellout.':'Baseline replay uses observed sales as demand. Sellout-day demand may be higher.';\n el('mixes').innerHTML=(expanded?mixes:mixes.slice(0,5)).map(x=>row([x.m,x.s,x.total,avg(x.sold),avg(x.waste),cash(x.net)],x===best?'best':'')).join('');\n el('more').textContent=expanded?'Show top 5 mixes':'Show all '+mixes.length+' mixes';\n const alt=mixes.find(x=>x.total===88&&x!==best);\n el('trade').textContent='Compared with '+alt.m+' muffins and '+alt.s+' scones, the starting mix earns '+cash(best.net-alt.net)+' more per market on average, with '+avg(best.waste)+' versus '+avg(alt.waste)+' unsold.';\n el('history').innerHTML=['Muffins','Scones'].map((p,k)=>{\n  const idx=k*2, baked=records.reduce((v,r)=>v+r[idx],0),sold=records.reduce((v,r)=>v+r[idx+1],0);\n  const sellouts=records.flatMap((r,i)=>r[idx]>0&&r[idx]===r[idx+1]?[i+1]:[]);\n  return row([p,baked,sold,baked-sold,baked?avg(100*(baked-sold)/baked)+'%':'—',cash(sold*[400,350][k]-baked*[120,105][k]),sellouts.length?'Market '+sellouts.join(', '):'None']);\n }).join('');\n el('n').textContent='Totals across '+days+' recorded markets. Waste is the number baked minus the number sold.';\n}\nfor(const name of ['rule','extra'])el(name).onchange=render;\nel('more').onclick=()=>{expanded=!expanded;render()};\nel('apply').onclick=()=>{\n const status=el('status');\n try{records=parseRecords(el('records').value)}catch(e){status.className='error';status.textContent=e.message;return}\n status.className='';render();\n try{localStorage.setItem(storageKey,el('records').value);status.textContent='Applied and saved in this browser.'}catch{status.textContent='Applied for this session. Copy your records to keep them.'}\n};\nrender();\n</script></html>\n"}],"download":"data/release/assets/aa03cb49db144b15210342142348800bbffe930a65ab323d4e20dd333b023d48.zip"},"807324c3dc4f68e7":{"files":[{"name":"market-planner.html","bytes":30019,"sha256":"86eec8c8ce0005fd8543e17149be53e6d020bda701722f58eb14e0cb0cacf4a5","kind":"text","body":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Saturday Market Planner</title>\n<style>\n  :root {\n    color-scheme: light;\n    --paper: #f8f3e9;\n    --surface: #fffdf8;\n    --ink: #2e211d;\n    --muted: #67534b;\n    --line: #ddcfc1;\n    --berry: #7e343f;\n    --blush: #f4e2df;\n    --sage: #e5eadb;\n    --green: #33482e;\n    --serif: Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n  }\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  body {\n    margin: 0;\n    background: var(--paper);\n    color: var(--ink);\n    font: 1rem/1.55 system-ui, sans-serif;\n  }\n  h1, h2, h3, p { margin: 0; }\n  h1, h2 { font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.05; }\n  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.65rem, 6vw, 4.65rem); letter-spacing: -.055em; }\n  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.85rem, 3vw, 2.6rem); letter-spacing: -.035em; }\n  h3 { font-size: 1rem; }\n  .wrap { width: min(1080px, calc(100% - 48px)); margin-inline: auto; }\n  header { border-top: 7px solid var(--berry); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n  .masthead { padding-block: 40px 32px; display: flex; gap: 20px; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; }\n  .masthead p { margin-top: 10px; color: var(--muted); }\n  main { padding-block: 34px 52px; }\n  .section-block, #plan-results:not([hidden]) + section, main > section + section { margin-top: 44px; }\n  .section-intro { margin-block: 8px 16px; color: var(--muted); max-width: 75ch; }\n  .grid, .summary-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 14px; }\n  .card, .panel { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; }\n  .card { padding: clamp(15px, 2.5vw, 25px); }\n  .panel { padding: clamp(14px, 2.5vw, 24px); }\n  .starting { color: #fffaf3; background: var(--berry); border-color: var(--berry); }\n  .alternate { background: var(--sage); border-color: #c8d2bc; color: var(--green); }\n  .eyebrow {\n    font-size: .76rem;\n    font-weight: 750;\n    letter-spacing: .11em;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n  }\n  .mix { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; margin-block: 8px 12px; gap: 12px; }\n  .mix strong { display: block; font: 400 clamp(2.55rem, 5vw, 4.35rem)/1 var(--serif); }\n  .mix small { display: block; font-size: .83rem; }\n  .capacity { font-size: .87rem; }\n  .metrics {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    gap: 8px 24px;\n    margin: 12px 0 0;\n    padding-top: 10px;\n    border-top: 1px solid currentColor;\n    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;\n  }\n  dt { font-size: .8rem; }\n  dd { margin: 0; font-weight: 730; }\n  .callout {\n    margin-top: 14px;\n    padding: 12px 16px;\n    border-left: 3px solid var(--berry);\n    background: var(--blush);\n  }\n  .toolbar { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 12px; }\n  .table-toolbar { justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 14px; }\n  .table-toolbar > div { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }\n  button, select, input { font: inherit; color: var(--ink); }\n  button, select {\n    background: var(--surface);\n    border: 1px solid #a3887e;\n    border-radius: 7px;\n    min-height: 44px;\n    padding: 7px 12px;\n  }\n  button { flex-shrink: 0; cursor: pointer; }\n  button:hover, select:hover { background: var(--blush); }\n  button:disabled { opacity: .55; cursor: default; }\n  :focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #225b85; outline-offset: 2px; }\n  input[type=\"number\"] {\n    background: var(--surface);\n    border: 1px solid #a3887e;\n    border-radius: 6px;\n    min-height: 44px;\n    padding: 5px 8px;\n    width: 100%;\n    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;\n  }\n  [aria-invalid=\"true\"] { outline: 2px solid var(--berry); outline-offset: -1px; }\n  table {\n    width: 100%;\n    border-collapse: collapse;\n    font-size: .91rem;\n    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;\n  }\n  caption { text-align: left; color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; margin-bottom: 6px; }\n  th, td { text-align: right; padding: 8px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n  thead th { font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.2; }\n  .col-group { text-align: center; background: var(--blush); }\n  .col-group + .col-group { background: var(--sage); }\n  .ranked td:first-child { font-weight: 750; }\n  tbody tr.leader { background: var(--blush); }\n  tbody tr:hover { background: #f6eee3; }\n  .history-name { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 400; }\n  .big-stat { font: 400 2.15rem/1.1 var(--serif); margin-top: 8px; }\n  .big-stat span { font: .86rem system-ui, sans-serif; color: var(--muted); }\n  .details-line { color: var(--muted); font-size: .87rem; margin-top: 8px; }\n  .history-table { table-layout: fixed; }\n  .history-table col:first-child { width: 13%; }\n  .history-table col:last-child { width: 15%; }\n  .history-table td { vertical-align: top; }\n  .history-table input { max-width: 106px; font-size: 1rem; appearance: textfield; }\n  .history-table input::-webkit-inner-spin-button { appearance: none; }\n  .history-table button { max-width: 100%; min-width: 44px; padding-inline: 8px; }\n  .flag { display: block; color: var(--berry); font-size: .73rem; font-weight: 730; }\n  .settings { border: 0; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 20px; min-width: 0; }\n  .settings legend { padding: 0; font-weight: 730; margin-bottom: 8px; }\n  .fields { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 12px 16px; }\n  .fields label { display: grid; align-content: end; gap: 4px; font-size: .88rem; }\n  .settings-help, .panel-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: .87rem; margin: 8px 0 0; }\n  .input-actions { margin-top: 10px; }\n  .total { margin-top: 10px; font-weight: 650; }\n  .notice { margin-bottom: 10px; }\n  .error { color: var(--berry); font-weight: 730; }\n  .status { margin-top: 8px; min-height: 1.5em; }\n  .method { padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }\n  .method p { margin-top: 8px; max-width: 85ch; }\n  [hidden] { display: none !important; }\n  @media (max-width: 650px) {\n    .wrap { width: calc(100% - 26px); }\n    .masthead { display: block; padding-block: 24px 19px; }\n    .masthead button { margin-top: 10px; }\n    main { padding-block: 24px 36px; }\n    .section-block, #plan-results:not([hidden]) + section, main > section + section { margin-top: 34px; }\n    .grid, .summary-grid { gap: 8px; }\n    .fields { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }\n    th, td { padding: 7px 4px; }\n    .history-table col:last-child { width: 52px; }\n    .history-table .remove-text { font-size: 0; }\n    .history-table .remove-text::after { content: \"×\"; font-size: 1.1rem; }\n    .history-table td input { padding-inline: 4px; }\n    .table-toolbar { align-items: start; }\n  }\n  @media (max-width: 385px) {\n    .ranked { font-size: .77rem; }\n    .ranked thead th { font-size: .72rem; }\n    .mix { gap: 6px; }\n    .card { padding: 12px; }\n  }\n  @media print {\n    body { background: white; color: black; font-size: .85rem; }\n    .wrap { width: 100%; }\n    .masthead, main { padding-block: 12px; }\n    .section-block, #plan-results:not([hidden]) + section, main > section + section { margin-top: 22px; }\n    .no-print, .history-table thead tr:first-child th:last-child, .history-table td:last-child { display: none !important; }\n    .history-table col:last-child { width: 0; }\n    .card, .callout { break-inside: avoid; }\n    .starting { color: black; background: white; border-color: var(--berry); }\n    .panel { padding: 9px; }\n    input[type=\"number\"] { min-height: 0; border: 0; appearance: textfield; }\n    input::-webkit-inner-spin-button { appearance: none; }\n    th, td { padding: 4px; }\n    tr { break-inside: avoid; }\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<header>\n  <div class=\"wrap masthead\">\n    <div>\n      <h1>Saturday Market Planner</h1>\n      <p>Batch planning for muffins and scones</p>\n    </div>\n    <button id=\"print\" class=\"no-print\" type=\"button\">Print plan</button>\n  </div>\n</header>\n<main class=\"wrap\">\n  <noscript><p class=\"notice error\">Enable JavaScript in your browser to calculate batch mixes.</p></noscript>\n  <p id=\"calculation-error\" class=\"notice error\" role=\"alert\" hidden></p>\n  <div id=\"plan-results\">\n    <section aria-labelledby=\"plan-title\">\n      <h2 id=\"plan-title\">What to bake</h2>\n      <p class=\"section-intro\" id=\"plan-context\"></p>\n      <div class=\"grid\">\n        <article id=\"baseline-card\" class=\"card starting\"></article>\n        <article id=\"uplift-card\" class=\"card alternate\"></article>\n      </div>\n      <p id=\"tradeoff\" class=\"callout\"></p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"section-block\" aria-labelledby=\"compare-title\">\n      <h2 id=\"compare-title\">Compare batch mixes</h2>\n      <p class=\"section-intro\">Contribution is sales revenue minus the cost of every item baked. Waste counts the units left over.</p>\n      <div class=\"panel\">\n        <div class=\"toolbar table-toolbar no-print\">\n          <div>\n            <label for=\"show-mixes\">Show</label>\n            <select id=\"show-mixes\">\n              <option value=\"top\">Top 8 mixes</option>\n              <option value=\"full\">Fullest loads</option>\n              <option value=\"all\">All feasible mixes</option>\n            </select>\n          </div>\n          <div>\n            <label for=\"rank-mixes\">Rank by</label>\n            <select id=\"rank-mixes\">\n              <option value=\"baseline\">Observed sales</option>\n              <option value=\"uplift\">Sellout uplift</option>\n            </select>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <table class=\"ranked\">\n          <caption id=\"mix-caption\"></caption>\n          <colgroup span=\"2\"></colgroup><colgroup span=\"2\"></colgroup><colgroup span=\"2\"></colgroup>\n          <thead>\n            <tr>\n              <th scope=\"col\" rowspan=\"2\">Muffins</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\" rowspan=\"2\">Scones</th>\n              <th scope=\"colgroup\" colspan=\"2\" class=\"col-group\">Observed sales</th>\n              <th scope=\"colgroup\" colspan=\"2\" class=\"col-group\">Sellout uplift</th>\n            </tr>\n            <tr>\n              <th scope=\"col\" id=\"baseline-sort\">Contrib.</th><th scope=\"col\">Waste</th>\n              <th scope=\"col\" id=\"uplift-sort\">Contrib.</th><th scope=\"col\">Waste</th>\n            </tr>\n          </thead>\n          <tbody id=\"mixes\"></tbody>\n        </table>\n        <p class=\"panel-note\">Ranks use unrounded averages. Ties favor fewer leftovers, then fewer total items, then fewer muffins.</p>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n\n  <section aria-labelledby=\"history-title\">\n    <h2 id=\"history-title\">Market history</h2>\n    <p class=\"section-intro\">The planner starts with six fictional Saturdays. A sellout tells you demand reached at least the number baked. Keep a tally of requests after a sellout to inform future batches.</p>\n    <div id=\"history-results\">\n      <div id=\"history-cards\" class=\"summary-grid\"></div>\n      <p class=\"total\" id=\"history-total\"></p>\n      <p class=\"panel-note\">Historical contribution uses the unit prices and costs entered below for every market.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"panel\" style=\"margin-top: 14px\">\n      <table class=\"history-table\">\n        <caption>Enter the number baked and sold at each market, oldest to newest.</caption>\n        <col><colgroup span=\"2\"></colgroup><colgroup span=\"2\"></colgroup><col>\n        <thead>\n          <tr>\n            <th rowspan=\"2\" scope=\"col\">Market</th>\n            <th colspan=\"2\" scope=\"colgroup\" class=\"col-group\">Muffins</th>\n            <th colspan=\"2\" scope=\"colgroup\" class=\"col-group\">Scones</th>\n            <th rowspan=\"2\" scope=\"col\"><span class=\"remove-text\">Remove</span></th>\n          </tr>\n          <tr>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Baked</th><th scope=\"col\">Sold</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Baked</th><th scope=\"col\">Sold</th>\n          </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody id=\"history\"></tbody>\n      </table>\n      <p id=\"history-error\" class=\"panel-note error\" role=\"alert\" hidden></p>\n      <div class=\"toolbar input-actions no-print\">\n        <button id=\"add-market\" type=\"button\">Add market</button>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <section aria-labelledby=\"settings-title\">\n    <h2 id=\"settings-title\">Planning inputs</h2>\n    <p class=\"section-intro\">Each product is baked in batches of eight. Unsold items earn zero revenue.</p>\n    <div class=\"panel\">\n      <fieldset class=\"settings\">\n        <legend>Capacity and unit economics</legend>\n        <div class=\"fields\">\n          <label>Capacity (items)<input id=\"capacity\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" max=\"400\" step=\"1\" required></label>\n          <label>Muffin price ($)<input id=\"muffin-price\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" max=\"9999.99\" step=\"0.01\" required></label>\n          <label>Muffin cost ($)<input id=\"muffin-cost\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" max=\"9999.99\" step=\"0.01\" required></label>\n          <label>Scone price ($)<input id=\"scone-price\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" max=\"9999.99\" step=\"0.01\" required></label>\n          <label>Scone cost ($)<input id=\"scone-cost\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" max=\"9999.99\" step=\"0.01\" required></label>\n        </div>\n      </fieldset>\n      <fieldset class=\"settings\">\n        <legend>Sellout uplift</legend>\n        <div class=\"fields\">\n          <label>Extra muffins per sellout<input id=\"muffin-uplift\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" max=\"9999\" step=\"1\" required aria-describedby=\"uplift-help\"></label>\n          <label>Extra scones per sellout<input id=\"scone-uplift\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" max=\"9999\" step=\"1\" required aria-describedby=\"uplift-help\"></label>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"settings-help\" id=\"uplift-help\">The starting assumption adds one batch of demand for the specific product on each day it sold out. Change the values to see when the preferred mix shifts.</p>\n      </fieldset>\n      <p id=\"settings-error\" class=\"panel-note error\" role=\"alert\" hidden></p>\n      <div class=\"toolbar no-print\">\n        <button id=\"save-plan\" type=\"button\">Save data file</button>\n        <button id=\"open-plan\" type=\"button\">Open data file</button>\n        <input type=\"file\" id=\"plan-file\" accept=\".json,application/json\" hidden>\n      </div>\n      <p id=\"save-status\" class=\"panel-note status no-print\" role=\"status\">Save a data file to carry your inputs to another browser or device.</p>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"method\" aria-labelledby=\"method-title\">\n    <h2 id=\"method-title\">How the planner scores a mix</h2>\n    <p><strong>Observed sales.</strong> Replay each market with the proposed quantities and use recorded sales as the demand proxy. Each product sells the smaller of its proposed bake quantity and that day’s recorded sales.</p>\n    <p><strong>Sellout uplift.</strong> Use the same replay and add the chosen extra demand on positive-quantity sellouts only. Both scenarios keep muffins and scones paired by market and average the included markets equally. Markets where either product was unavailable are excluded from the mix replay, while historical totals include every row.</p>\n    <p>These are scenario averages from a small history. Weather, seasonality and changes in market traffic can shift demand. The uplift is an assumption for testing the bake plan’s sensitivity to missed sales.</p>\n  </section>\n</main>\n<script>\n\"use strict\";\n\nconst BATCH = 8;\nconst PRODUCTS = [\"Muffins\", \"Scones\"];\nconst HISTORY_FIELDS = [\"muffins baked\", \"muffins sold\", \"scones baked\", \"scones sold\"];\nconst SETTING_IDS = [\n  \"capacity\", \"muffin-price\", \"muffin-cost\", \"scone-price\", \"scone-cost\", \"muffin-uplift\", \"scone-uplift\"\n];\nconst INITIAL = {\n  version: 1,\n  settings: [88, 4, 1.2, 3.5, 1.05, 8, 8],\n  history: [\n    [40, 35, 32, 28], [40, 40, 32, 30], [48, 45, 32, 32],\n    [48, 48, 40, 35], [56, 49, 40, 34], [56, 52, 40, 38]\n  ]\n};\n\nconst $ = id => document.getElementById(id);\nconst storageKey = \"saturday-market-planner-v1\";\nconst dollars = new Intl.NumberFormat(\"en-US\", { style: \"currency\", currency: \"USD\" });\nconst decimal = new Intl.NumberFormat(\"en-US\", { minimumFractionDigits: 1, maximumFractionDigits: 1 });\nconst money = cents => dollars.format(cents / 100);\nconst inputNumber = input => input.value === \"\" ? NaN : Number(input.value);\nconst unitWord = n => n === 1 ? \"item\" : \"items\";\nconst sellout = (baked, sold) => baked > 0 && sold === baked;\nconst whole = (n, max) => Number.isInteger(n) && n >= 0 && n <= max;\nconst validMoney = n => Number.isFinite(n) && n >= 0 && n <= 9999.99 && Number(n.toFixed(2)) === n;\n\nfunction validData(data) {\n  if (data?.version !== 1 || !Array.isArray(data.settings) || data.settings.length !== 7 ||\n      !Array.isArray(data.history)) return false;\n  const [capacity, ...rest] = data.settings;\n  const [muffinPrice, muffinCost, sconePrice, sconeCost, muffinUplift, sconeUplift] = rest;\n  return whole(capacity, 400) &&\n    [muffinPrice, muffinCost, sconePrice, sconeCost].every(validMoney) &&\n    [muffinUplift, sconeUplift].every(n => whole(n, 9999)) &&\n    data.history.every(row => Array.isArray(row) && row.length === 4 &&\n      row.every(n => whole(n, 9999)) && row[1] <= row[0] && row[3] <= row[2]);\n}\n\nfunction historicalTotals(history, prices, costs) {\n  return PRODUCTS.map((name, i) => {\n    let baked = 0;\n    let sold = 0;\n    let sellouts = 0;\n    for (const row of history) {\n      baked += row[2 * i];\n      sold += row[2 * i + 1];\n      sellouts += Number(sellout(row[2 * i], row[2 * i + 1]));\n    }\n    const waste = baked - sold;\n    return { name, baked, sold, waste, sellouts, wasteCost: waste * costs[i],\n      contribution: sold * prices[i] - baked * costs[i] };\n  });\n}\n\nfunction scoreMix(muffins, scones, demand, prices, costs) {\n  const bakeCost = muffins * costs[0] + scones * costs[1];\n  let contribution = 0;\n  let waste = 0;\n  for (const [muffinDemand, sconeDemand] of demand) {\n    const muffinsSold = Math.min(muffins, muffinDemand);\n    const sconesSold = Math.min(scones, sconeDemand);\n    contribution += muffinsSold * prices[0] + sconesSold * prices[1] - bakeCost;\n    waste += muffins + scones - muffinsSold - sconesSold;\n  }\n  return { contribution, waste };\n}\n\nfunction evaluateMixes(history, capacity, prices, costs, uplift) {\n  const eligible = history.filter(row => row[0] > 0 && row[2] > 0);\n  const observed = eligible.map(row => [row[1], row[3]]);\n  const adjusted = eligible.map(row => [\n    row[1] + (sellout(row[0], row[1]) ? uplift[0] : 0),\n    row[3] + (sellout(row[2], row[3]) ? uplift[1] : 0)\n  ]);\n  const mixes = [];\n  for (let muffins = 0; muffins <= capacity; muffins += BATCH) {\n    for (let scones = 0; scones <= capacity - muffins; scones += BATCH) {\n      mixes.push({\n        muffins, scones, total: muffins + scones,\n        baseline: scoreMix(muffins, scones, observed, prices, costs),\n        uplift: scoreMix(muffins, scones, adjusted, prices, costs)\n      });\n    }\n  }\n  return { mixes, count: eligible.length };\n}\n\nfunction byScore(scenario) {\n  return (a, b) => b[scenario].contribution - a[scenario].contribution ||\n    a[scenario].waste - b[scenario].waste || a.total - b.total || a.muffins - b.muffins;\n}\n\nfunction showMessage(element, message) {\n  element.textContent = message;\n  element.hidden = !message;\n}\n\nfunction renderHistory(history) {\n  $(\"history\").innerHTML = history.map((row, i) => `\n    <tr>\n      <th scope=\"row\">${i + 1}</th>\n      ${row.map((quantity, field) => `<td>\n        <input type=\"number\" min=\"0\" max=\"9999\" step=\"1\" required\n          aria-label=\"Market ${i + 1}, ${HISTORY_FIELDS[field]}\" value=\"${quantity}\">\n        ${field % 2 === 1 ? '<span class=\"flag\" hidden>Sellout</span>' : \"\"}\n      </td>`).join(\"\")}\n      <td><button type=\"button\" data-remove=\"${i}\" aria-label=\"Remove market ${i + 1}\">\n        <span class=\"remove-text\">Remove</span></button></td>\n    </tr>`).join(\"\");\n}\n\nfunction readInputs() {\n  const history = [];\n  let historyError = \"\";\n  let settingsError = \"\";\n  for (const [i, row] of Array.from($(\"history\").rows).entries()) {\n    const inputs = [...row.querySelectorAll(\"input\")];\n    const quantities = inputs.map(inputNumber);\n    inputs.forEach((input, field) => {\n      const exceedsBaked = field % 2 === 1 && quantities[field] > quantities[field - 1];\n      const invalid = !whole(quantities[field], Number(input.max)) || exceedsBaked;\n      input.setAttribute(\"aria-invalid\", String(invalid));\n      if (invalid) {\n        historyError ||= exceedsBaked\n          ? `Market ${i + 1}: ${HISTORY_FIELDS[field]} cannot exceed the number baked.`\n          : `Market ${i + 1}: enter a whole number from 0 to 9,999 for ${HISTORY_FIELDS[field]}.`;\n      }\n      const flag = input.nextElementSibling;\n      if (flag) flag.hidden = invalid || !sellout(quantities[field - 1], quantities[field]);\n    });\n    history.push(quantities);\n  }\n  const settings = SETTING_IDS.map(id => {\n    const input = $(id);\n    const value = inputNumber(input);\n    const isMoney = input.step === \"0.01\";\n    const valid = isMoney ? validMoney(value) : whole(value, Number(input.max));\n    input.setAttribute(\"aria-invalid\", String(!valid));\n    if (!valid) {\n      const label = input.labels[0].textContent.trim();\n      const range = isMoney ? \"a dollar amount from 0 to 9,999.99 with at most two decimal places\"\n        : `a whole number from 0 to ${Number(input.max).toLocaleString(\"en-US\")}`;\n      settingsError ||= `${label}: enter ${range}.`;\n    }\n    return value;\n  });\n  showMessage($(\"history-error\"), historyError);\n  showMessage($(\"settings-error\"), settingsError);\n  return historyError || settingsError ? null : { version: 1, settings, history };\n}\n\nfunction renderHistoryTotals(totals) {\n  $(\"history-cards\").innerHTML = totals.map(t => `\n    <article class=\"card\">\n      <h3 class=\"history-name\">${t.name}</h3>\n      <p class=\"big-stat\">${t.waste} <span>left over · ${t.baked ? decimal.format(100 * t.waste / t.baked) + \"% of bake\" : \"zero baked\"}</span></p>\n      <p class=\"details-line\">${t.sold} sold of ${t.baked} baked · ${t.sellouts} ${t.sellouts === 1 ? \"sellout\" : \"sellouts\"}</p>\n      <dl class=\"metrics\">\n        <div><dt>Contribution</dt><dd>${money(t.contribution)}</dd></div>\n        <div><dt>Cost of leftovers</dt><dd>${money(t.wasteCost)}</dd></div>\n      </dl>\n    </article>`).join(\"\");\n  const waste = totals.reduce((sum, t) => sum + t.waste, 0);\n  const contribution = totals.reduce((sum, t) => sum + t.contribution, 0);\n  $(\"history-total\").textContent = `Combined: ${waste} leftover ${unitWord(waste)} · ${money(contribution)} contribution`;\n}\n\nfunction renderCard(id, title, best, scenario, count, capacity) {\n  const score = best[scenario];\n  const batches = n => `${n / BATCH} ${n === BATCH ? \"batch\" : \"batches\"}`;\n  const spare = capacity - best.total;\n  $(id).innerHTML = `\n    <h3 class=\"eyebrow\">${title}</h3>\n    <div class=\"mix\">\n      <div><strong>${best.muffins}</strong>Muffins<small>${batches(best.muffins)}</small></div>\n      <div><strong>${best.scones}</strong>Scones<small>${batches(best.scones)}</small></div>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"capacity\">${best.total} of ${capacity} slots used · ${spare} spare</p>\n    <dl class=\"metrics\">\n      <div><dt>Avg. contribution</dt><dd>${money(score.contribution / count)}</dd></div>\n      <div><dt>Avg. leftovers</dt><dd>${decimal.format(score.waste / count)}</dd></div>\n    </dl>`;\n}\n\nfunction renderMixTable() {\n  if (!results) return;\n  const { mixes, count } = results;\n  const scenario = $(\"rank-mixes\").value;\n  const filter = $(\"show-mixes\").value;\n  let ranked = mixes.slice().sort(byScore(scenario));\n  if (filter === \"top\") ranked = ranked.slice(0, 8);\n  if (filter === \"full\") {\n    const fullest = Math.max(...mixes.map(mix => mix.total));\n    ranked = ranked.filter(mix => mix.total === fullest);\n  }\n  $(\"mix-caption\").textContent = `${ranked.length} of ${mixes.length} feasible mixes. Averages per market, ranked by ${scenario === \"baseline\" ? \"observed sales\" : \"sellout uplift\"} contribution.`;\n  $(\"baseline-sort\").setAttribute(\"aria-sort\", scenario === \"baseline\" ? \"descending\" : \"none\");\n  $(\"uplift-sort\").setAttribute(\"aria-sort\", scenario === \"uplift\" ? \"descending\" : \"none\");\n  $(\"mixes\").innerHTML = ranked.map((mix, i) => `<tr${i === 0 ? ' class=\"leader\"' : \"\"}>\n    <td>${mix.muffins}</td><td>${mix.scones}</td>\n    <td>${money(mix.baseline.contribution / count)}</td><td>${decimal.format(mix.baseline.waste / count)}</td>\n    <td>${money(mix.uplift.contribution / count)}</td><td>${decimal.format(mix.uplift.waste / count)}</td>\n  </tr>`).join(\"\");\n}\n\nfunction renderPlan(data) {\n  const [capacity, muffinPrice, muffinCost, sconePrice, sconeCost, ...uplift] = data.settings;\n  const prices = [Math.round(100 * muffinPrice), Math.round(100 * sconePrice)];\n  const costs = [Math.round(100 * muffinCost), Math.round(100 * sconeCost)];\n  renderHistoryTotals(historicalTotals(data.history, prices, costs));\n  results = evaluateMixes(data.history, capacity, prices, costs, uplift);\n  const { mixes, count } = results;\n  $(\"plan-results\").hidden = count === 0;\n  if (count === 0) {\n    showMessage($(\"calculation-error\"), \"Enter at least one market where both products were baked to compare batch mixes.\");\n    return;\n  }\n  const baseline = mixes.slice().sort(byScore(\"baseline\"))[0];\n  const alternate = mixes.slice().sort(byScore(\"uplift\"))[0];\n  const skipped = data.history.length - count;\n  $(\"plan-context\").textContent = `${count} paired ${count === 1 ? \"market\" : \"markets\"} replayed · ${capacity}-item cap · batches of ${BATCH}.` +\n    (skipped ? ` ${skipped} ${skipped === 1 ? \"market lacked\" : \"markets lacked\"} a bake quantity for one or both products and ${skipped === 1 ? \"was\" : \"were\"} excluded.` : \"\");\n  renderCard(\"baseline-card\", \"Starting bake · observed sales\", baseline, \"baseline\", count, capacity);\n  renderCard(\"uplift-card\", \"Best mix · sellout uplift\", alternate, \"uplift\", count, capacity);\n  const baselineGap = (baseline.baseline.contribution - alternate.baseline.contribution) / count;\n  const alternateGap = (alternate.uplift.contribution - baseline.uplift.contribution) / count;\n  const upliftText = `Uplift adds ${uplift[0]} muffins or ${uplift[1]} scones of demand on each respective historical sellout.`;\n  const observedWasteGap = (alternate.baseline.waste - baseline.baseline.waste) / count;\n  const upliftWasteGap = (alternate.uplift.waste - baseline.uplift.waste) / count;\n  const wasteChange = gap => Math.abs(gap) < .05 ? \"the same average leftovers\" :\n    `${decimal.format(Math.abs(gap))} ${gap > 0 ? \"more\" : \"fewer\"} leftovers on average`;\n  $(\"tradeoff\").textContent = baseline === alternate\n    ? `${upliftText} The same mix leads in both replays.`\n    : `${upliftText} Compared with the starting bake, the uplift mix earns ${money(baselineGap)} less per market with observed sales and ${money(alternateGap)} more with uplift. It has ${wasteChange(observedWasteGap)} with observed sales and ${wasteChange(upliftWasteGap)} with uplift.`;\n  renderMixTable();\n}\n\nfunction update() {\n  const data = readInputs();\n  $(\"save-plan\").disabled = data === null;\n  $(\"plan-results\").hidden = data === null;\n  $(\"history-results\").hidden = data === null;\n  showMessage($(\"calculation-error\"), data ? \"\" : \"Correct the highlighted inputs to recalculate the plan.\");\n  if (!data) {\n    results = null;\n    return;\n  }\n  renderPlan(data);\n  try {\n    localStorage.setItem(storageKey, JSON.stringify(data));\n  } catch {\n    // The data file remains available when browser storage is disabled.\n  }\n}\n\nfunction loadInputs(data) {\n  SETTING_IDS.forEach((id, i) => {\n    const input = $(id);\n    input.value = input.step === \"0.01\" ? data.settings[i].toFixed(2) : data.settings[i];\n  });\n  renderHistory(data.history);\n  update();\n}\n\nfunction currentRowValues() {\n  return [...$(\"history\").rows].map(row => [...row.querySelectorAll(\"input\")].map(input => input.value));\n}\n\nlet results = null;\nlet initialData = INITIAL;\ntry {\n  const saved = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(storageKey));\n  if (validData(saved)) initialData = saved;\n} catch {\n  // Start from the supplied history when storage is unavailable or unreadable.\n}\nloadInputs(initialData);\n\ndocument.addEventListener(\"input\", event => {\n  if (event.target.matches('input[type=\"number\"]')) update();\n});\n$(\"show-mixes\").addEventListener(\"change\", renderMixTable);\n$(\"rank-mixes\").addEventListener(\"change\", renderMixTable);\n$(\"add-market\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n  const history = currentRowValues();\n  history.push([\"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"]);\n  renderHistory(history);\n  update();\n  $(\"history\").rows[history.length - 1].querySelector(\"input\").focus();\n});\n$(\"history\").addEventListener(\"click\", event => {\n  const button = event.target.closest(\"[data-remove]\");\n  if (!button) return;\n  const i = Number(button.dataset.remove);\n  const history = currentRowValues();\n  history.splice(i, 1);\n  renderHistory(history);\n  update();\n  const nextRow = $(\"history\").rows[Math.min(i, history.length - 1)];\n  (nextRow?.querySelector(\"button\") || $(\"add-market\")).focus();\n});\n$(\"print\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => window.print());\n$(\"save-plan\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n  const data = readInputs();\n  if (!data) return;\n  const file = new Blob([JSON.stringify(data, null, 2) + \"\\n\"], { type: \"application/json\" });\n  const url = URL.createObjectURL(file);\n  const link = document.createElement(\"a\");\n  link.href = url;\n  link.download = \"market-planner-data.json\";\n  link.click();\n  setTimeout(() => URL.revokeObjectURL(url), 1000);\n  $(\"save-status\").textContent = \"Data file downloaded. Open it here to restore your markets and settings.\";\n});\n$(\"open-plan\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => $(\"plan-file\").click());\n$(\"plan-file\").addEventListener(\"change\", async event => {\n  const file = event.target.files[0];\n  event.target.value = \"\";\n  if (!file) return;\n  try {\n    const data = JSON.parse(await file.text());\n    if (!validData(data)) throw new Error(\"Invalid plan\");\n    loadInputs(data);\n    $(\"save-status\").textContent = \"Markets and settings restored from the data file.\";\n  } catch {\n    $(\"save-status\").textContent = \"Could not open this file. Choose a valid market planner data file.\";\n  }\n});\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}],"download":"data/release/assets/69f14c67e3e82db50ac8fb5f469e898754b7bc1f6e895d1370a90dbdea86cda9.zip"}}}
